The Iron Man Mark XLV (45) suit makes its appearance during the final battle of Sokovia in Avengers: Age of Ultron, debuting as Tony Stark's first armor to sport a distinctly organic, muscular aesthetic with sweeping ergonomic lines rather than traditional blocky plating. Beyond its visually striking hexagonal-bordered circular Unibeam housing and deep crimson-and-gold finish, the Mark XLV was the very first suit to integrate F.R.I.D.A.Y.—Tony’s Irish-accented user interface software—as his main tactical AI following the ascension of JARVIS into the Vision. Engineered specifically for extreme heat resistance and energy dispersal, the suit survived high-temperature energy amplification from Vision and Thor to vaporize Ultron’s vibranium core, while wielding enhanced repulsors capable of cutting through entire waves of Ultron sentries in rapid succession.
